From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Reckmann <robin.reckmann@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 05:44:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: dispcc-sdm845: avoid enabling DSI PLL during probe

Commit a1d63493634e ("clk: qcom: dispcc-sdm845: Enable parents for pixel
clocks") set CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE on the two DSI pixel clock sources.
With that flag the clock framework enables the parent around a
reparent, including when it adopts orphans while the DSI PHY registers
its PLL at probe. On SDM845 that parent is the 10nm DSI PLL, and
enabling it before the PHY has been initialised can make the PLL fail
to lock.

Drop the flag again for SDM845. The DSI host and MDSS paths prepare and
enable the PLL themselves when they need it, after the PHY is set up.

Fixes: a1d63493634e ("clk: qcom: dispcc-sdm845: Enable parents for pixel clocks")
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sdm845.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sdm845.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sdm845.c
index 5df2893f56..f371edc881 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sdm845.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sdm845.c
@@ -279,7 +279,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 disp_cc_mdss_pclk0_clk_src = {
 		.name = "disp_cc_mdss_pclk0_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = disp_cc_parent_data_4,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(disp_cc_parent_data_4),
-		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE,
+		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
 		.ops = &clk_pixel_ops,
 	},
 };
@@ -294,7 +294,7 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 disp_cc_mdss_pclk1_clk_src = {
 		.name = "disp_cc_mdss_pclk1_clk_src",
 		.parent_data = disp_cc_parent_data_4,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(disp_cc_parent_data_4),
-		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE,
+		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
 		.ops = &clk_pixel_ops,
 	},
 };
